{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Whoever sacrifices to elohim.</b> To any divinity whatsoever, even though among them he may intend to include the blessed El as well." "<b>Shall be destroyed.</b> From soul to flesh, for they are חֵרֶם — all forbidden for benefit; and from the aspect that they accepted upon themselves a deity, the one who accepts is the חֵרֶם spoken of in them, as it says: וְהָיִיתָ חֵרֶם כָּמֹהוּ (Deuteronomy 7:26)." "<b>To YHWH alone.</b> Without association of other elohim."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:47.450244886Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}